\f0\b\fs48 \cf0 \strokec2 8. Introduction Script\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 When the participant arrives, say:\
\'93Thank you for helping me test my prototype.\
This is a university design project evaluating an XR interaction prototype.\
Today I would like you to complete a few short tasks using a Meta Quest headset.\
I am testing the design, not testing you, so there are no right or wrong answers. If something is difficult or confusing, that is useful information for my evaluation.\
I will mainly observe how you interact with the prototype. You do not need to explain everything you are thinking while you use it.\
After you finish the tasks, I will ask you four short questions about your experience.\
The session should only take around 10 to 15 minutes.\
If you feel uncomfortable, dizzy, or want to stop at any point, please tell me immediately.\
Is that okay?\'94\
Wait for confirmation before continuing.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \strokec3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa321\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs48 \cf0 \strokec2 9. VR Safety and Setup\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 Before giving the participant the headset, say:\
\'93Before we start, please stay within this testing area while wearing the headset.\
You do not need to walk very far.\
If at any point you feel uncomfortable or dizzy, please let me know and we will stop.\'94\
Help the participant put on the headset.\
Adjust the headset if necessary.\
Give the participant the controllers.\
Say:\
\'93Please take a few seconds to look around and get comfortable with the headset and controllers.\'94\
Allow approximately 20\'9630 seconds.\
Do not explain the interaction unless necessary.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \strokec3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa321\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs48 \cf0 \strokec2 10. Task Instructions\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 The participant will complete four tasks.\
The researcher should read each task individually.\
Do not explain how to complete the task unless the participant requires help.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \strokec3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 \strokec2 Task 1 \'96 Identify an Interactive Note\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 Say:\
\'93First, please look around the environment and identify something that you think you can interact with.\'94\
Observe:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 how quickly the participant identifies a note;\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 whether they look at irrelevant objects;\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 whether they appear confused;\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 whether they ask what is interactive.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 Record:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 success/failure;\
\ls3\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 errors;\
\ls3\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 assistance;\
\ls3\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 observations.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 Do not immediately tell them what to select.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \strokec3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 \strokec2 Task 2 \'96 Select the Note\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 Say:\
\'93Now, please try to select or pick up the note you identified.\'94\
Do not initially tell them which controller button to press.\
Observe:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls4\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 whether they naturally try the trigger;\
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 whether they press incorrect buttons;\
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 how many attempts are required;\
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 whether they understand when the note has been selected.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 If they cannot proceed after several attempts, provide minimal assistance.\
Example assistance:\
\'93You can try using the trigger button.\'94\
Record this as one researcher intervention.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \strokec3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 \strokec2 Task 3 \'96 Interact With the Note\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 Say:\
\'93Now please interact with or manipulate the selected note.\'94\
Depending on the final prototype, this may include:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls5\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 moving the note;\
\ls5\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 holding the note;\
\ls5\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 repositioning it;\
\ls5\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 completing the intended note interaction.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 Observe:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls6\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 whether the participant understands what to do;\
\ls6\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 accidental interactions;\
\ls6\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 repeated attempts;\
\ls6\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 hesitation;\
\ls6\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 loss of selection;\
\ls6\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 need for assistance.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \strokec3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 \strokec2 Task 4 \'96 Complete the Interaction\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 Say:\
\'93Now please finish the interaction and leave the note in the way you think is correct.\'94\
Observe:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls7\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 whether the participant understands how to finish;\
\ls7\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 whether they successfully release or place the note;\
\ls7\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 whether feedback is clear;\
\ls7\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 whether they ask if the task has finished.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 When complete, say:\
\'93Great, that finishes the task section.\'94\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
